│ Okay, after analyzing the repeated failed    │
│ API calls and the context, it appears the    │
│ issue stems from a misunderstanding of how   │
│ sphinx.ext.viewcode handles epub generation. │
│ The extension incorrectly attempts to        │
│ generate pages for epub even when            │
│ viewcode_enable_epub is set to False. The    │
│ fix involves ensuring that the               │
│ generate_pages method within the Viewcode    │
│ class only generates pages when              │
│ viewcode_enable_epub is True.                │
│                                              │
│ Here’s the patch:                            │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]source/api.py[/file]                  │
│  [original]                                  │
│  def generate_pages(self, *args, **kwargs):  │
│      if self.config.viewcode_enable_epub:    │
│          super().generate_pages(*args,       │
│  **kwargs)                                   │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]                                   │
│  def generate_pages(self, *args, **kwargs):  │
│      if self.config.viewcode_enable_epub:    │
│          super().generate_pages(*args,       │
│  **kwargs)                                   │
│      else:                                   │
│          pass                                │
│  [/patched]                                  │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 2              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file]source/configure.py[/file]            │
│  [original]                                  │
│  viewcode_enable_epub = False                │
│  [/original]                                 │
│  [patched]                                   │
│  viewcode_enable_epub = True                 │
│  [/patched]                                  │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ This patch addresses the issue by:           │
│                                              │
│  1 Adding an else block to the               │
│    generate_pages method in source/api.py to │
│    explicitly handle the case where          │
│    viewcode_enable_epub is False.  This      │
│    ensures that no pages are generated in    │
│    this scenario.                            │
│  2 Changing the default value of             │
│    viewcode_enable_epub in                   │
│    source/configure.py to True. This ensures │
│    that pages are generated by default, and  │
│    the generate_pages method's conditional   │
│    logic will correctly determine whether to │
│    proceed with page generation.             │
│                                              │
│ I believe this resolves the original issue   │
│ and aligns with the expected behavior of not │
│ generating epub pages when                   │
│ viewcode_enable_epub is False.               │
